  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting sustainable economic growth in the Indian Ocean through improved engagement in fisheries management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the activity is to support the sustainable economic growth of Indian Ocean countries by increasing their capacity to influence the development of fisheries conservation and management measures (CMMs) by unifying the like-minded Indian Ocean coastal States (G16) to cooperatively engage in regional fisheries management negotiations. The activity will also seek to improve States&#x2019; compliance with conservation and management measures from the Indian Ocean Tuna Commission (IOTC) and support the G16. These efforts focus on small island and developing states in the Indian Ocean region, including but not limited to Bangladesh, Comoros, India, Indonesia, Kenya, Madagascar, Malaysia, Maldives, Mauritius, Mozambique, Oman, Pakistan, Seychelles, Somalia, the Republic of South Africa, Sri Lanka, Tanzania and Thailand.</narrative>
  </description>
